  "notes": [
    "Every sha256 is the real digest of the committed fixture bytes; tools/check-fixtures.mjs recomputes all of them.",
    "Envelope fixtures are standalone documents: projectId == directory name is a load-time check and is not asserted here.",
    "source-preimages/cue-start.wav is a real 48 kHz mono 16-bit PCM WAV (96 samples, 236 bytes, sha256 6228ba11eab4d769d9683d18dac12a3f23f9b23ed58e133ab24a6ac75ea5effb). The audio AssetRecord importRecipe/metrics fields in catalog/audio-asset-record-v3.json, envelope/valid/demo-0003-media-v3.json and envelope/invalid/cue-kind-mismatch.json are the real presentation.md §41.4.3 profile (recipe { profile: pcm-wav, recipeVersion: 1, toolchain { asset-pipeline: 0.1.0 } }, PcmWavMetrics frames 96 / durationMs 2 / pcmBytes 192) derived from that preimage by packet 47 (CC-44-2).",
    "model/modelAnimation role bindings in envelope/valid/demo-0003-media-v3.json are packet-41 placeholders: 39 fixes only the three role keys, requiredness, the assetId/version binding and the byte bound.",
    "Invalid fixtures isolate one rule each; check-fixtures.mjs re-derives the expected result independently for the version-combination, registry, reference, count and field rules it can and otherwise asserts the declared expectation and code.",
    "Expected results for envelope-level refusals are single errors; deeper checks stop (storage.md §S2/S4).",
    "The command scenario is replayed from recorded change data (contract consistency): revision/history arithmetic, derived-ID allocation, inverse/redo equality and the final document are re-derived.",
    "CC-44-3 repair (2026-09-19): `migration/v2-source/envelope.json` is a genuinely v2-loadable scene. It declared `schemaVersion: 2` while carrying the v3-only `cameraFollow` component, contradicting storage.md §16.5.1; the component was removed from the source and (verbatim carry) from the destination, and the checker now re-derives that a v2 source carries no v3-only component. No contract rule was relaxed: §23.11 clarifies that the v3-registry superset claim covers every v2-valid entity, not a v2 document carrying v3 components.",
    "CC-44-4 repair (2026-09-19): the migration destination is loadable. workspace.md §16.5.2 now resets the derived revision metadata on copy (`publishedRevision`, `behaviors[i].source.publishedRevision`, `behaviorTrust[].acknowledgedRevision` → 0) because the destination is a new project identity whose revision restarts at 0; the destination fixture's asset `publishedRevision` moved 2 → 0 and the checker re-derives the reset and the loadability."
  ],
